1
00:00:12,137 --> 00:00:13,806
[OLRUGGIO]
Mind you don't drop that bundle.

2
00:00:13,848 --> 00:00:14,974
As if I would.

3
00:00:16,057 --> 00:00:17,392
[DAGDA] Sir Witch!

4
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:19,895
The bridge was just past
that tall pine!

5
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,319
[AGOTT] Please allow me
to come along!

6
00:00:27,361 --> 00:00:30,155
I will be of use to you.
I promise.

7
00:00:32,199 --> 00:00:33,617
You can't.

8
00:00:34,368 --> 00:00:35,786
This isn't something
your training

9
00:00:35,828 --> 00:00:37,162
has prepared you for.

10
00:00:37,204 --> 00:00:39,832
There'll be many people there
who aren't witches.

11
00:00:40,374 --> 00:00:42,459
And since you've not taken
your second test yet,

12
00:00:42,501 --> 00:00:44,628
you aren't allowed
to cast in front of them.

13
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:46,005
So try to understand.

14
00:00:46,129 --> 00:00:48,173
- I promise you, one day I will--
- [Agott grunts softly]

15
00:00:48,215 --> 00:00:50,551
[AGOTT] When exactly
will that day be?

16
00:00:51,010 --> 00:00:52,761
I practice constantly on my own.

17
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:55,180
I know how to cast in public.

18
00:00:55,222 --> 00:00:57,933
And I've been preparing
for the test for ages now!

19
00:00:58,642 --> 00:00:59,977
As my teacher,

20
00:01:00,019 --> 00:01:02,145
are you not meant to seek out
chances for me

21
00:01:02,187 --> 00:01:03,772
to gain more experience?

22
00:01:04,231 --> 00:01:05,858
Yes, but even so.

23
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,359
[DAGDA] Please, there's no time!

24
00:01:07,401 --> 00:01:09,028
- [horse neighs]
- Whatever you do,

25
00:01:09,068 --> 00:01:10,404
we need to hurry!

26
00:01:10,863 --> 00:01:12,364
[OLRUGGIO] I'll go on ahead.

27
00:01:12,406 --> 00:01:13,782
Once I get onsite,

28
00:01:13,824 --> 00:01:15,951
I'll set up an exit
for the Windowway.

29
00:01:17,578 --> 00:01:20,079
You prepare the contraptions
and medicine we'll need.

30
00:01:20,873 --> 00:01:22,416
Agott can ride with me.

31
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:23,417
[Agott exclaims]

32
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:26,169
[AGOTT]
I'll fetch my cloak and hat!

33
00:01:29,048 --> 00:01:31,132
- We're coming, too!
- [Qifrey exclaims softly]

34
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:36,055
Ease up a bit, Qifrey.

35
00:01:36,095 --> 00:01:39,641
Some things can only be learned
through hands-on experience.

36
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:41,977
But I still worry.

37
00:01:42,436 --> 00:01:44,396
Especially about Agott.

38
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:46,982
She takes little joy
from her achievements.

39
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:49,944
Fixates on her limitations.

40
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:55,074
It's no crime
to lack experience.

41
00:01:55,114 --> 00:01:56,491
[Agott pants]

42
00:01:56,533 --> 00:01:58,577
[QIFREY] But she is racing
to grow up.

43
00:01:58,619 --> 00:01:59,620
[Agott grunts]

44
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:04,165
[QIFREY] So if she missteps,
she'll fall hard.

45
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,836
- [horse neighs]
- [Olruggio and Agott grunt]

46
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:11,256
The ground looks
none too stable.

47
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:14,051
[DAGDA] It's here.
It's still here.

48
00:02:30,317 --> 00:02:32,611
[♪ opening theme song playing]

49
00:04:02,534 --> 00:04:04,661
[indistinct chatter]

50
00:04:04,703 --> 00:04:07,206
[MAN 1] Oh, look! He's back!

51
00:04:07,915 --> 00:04:09,499
And he brought witches!

52
00:04:09,541 --> 00:04:11,501
- [men gasp]
- What a relief.

53
00:04:11,543 --> 00:04:12,711
They came just in time.

54
00:04:12,753 --> 00:04:15,130
Hey! Don't worry,
the witches are here!

55
00:04:15,172 --> 00:04:17,424
- [OLRUGGIO] Agott.
- [indistinct chatter]

56
00:04:17,465 --> 00:04:19,927
[OLRUGGIO] You know
how to use them, I take it?

57
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:23,138
Help these people
dry off their clothes.

58
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:25,724
- Then await further orders.
- [Agott grunts]

59
00:04:26,683 --> 00:04:29,394
You just want me to use
a simple contraption.

60
00:04:29,436 --> 00:04:31,897
Nothing else?
But I can do more--

61
00:04:31,939 --> 00:04:33,272
[OLRUGGIO] That's all I need.

62
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:35,274
Come now.

63
00:04:35,316 --> 00:04:36,693
What's the problem?

64
00:04:37,444 --> 00:04:40,072
You don't think simple tasks
are worth doing?

65
00:04:40,864 --> 00:04:43,117
I can see why Qifrey
was worried then.

66
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:46,120
Agott...

67
00:04:47,412 --> 00:04:49,164
You're too impatient by half.

68
00:04:49,206 --> 00:04:50,457
[Agott grunts softly]

69
00:04:51,290 --> 00:04:52,876
[OLRUGGIO] If you wish
to flaunt your skills,

70
00:04:52,918 --> 00:04:55,670
there are times
and places for that.

71
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:59,466
However, if you truly wish to be
useful here and now,

72
00:04:59,507 --> 00:05:03,720
you should take a moment
to reconsider what magic is for.

73
00:05:08,183 --> 00:05:09,476
- [OLRUGGIO] Aye up.
- [AGOTT] Yet again...

74
00:05:09,517 --> 00:05:10,727
[QIFREY] Thank you, Olly.

75
00:05:10,894 --> 00:05:13,188
[AGOTT]... I'm treated
like an ignorant child.

76
00:05:13,230 --> 00:05:15,816
I work harder than anyone,

77
00:05:16,191 --> 00:05:18,193
and I have nothing
to show for it.

78
00:05:18,986 --> 00:05:21,780
There's someone I need
to prove myself to.

79
00:05:22,864 --> 00:05:26,451
I will silence all doubt
that I'm a worthy witch.

80
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:32,791
[OLRUGGIO] Qifrey!

81
00:05:33,792 --> 00:05:34,918
[Qifrey grunting]

82
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:37,671
♪

83
00:05:39,256 --> 00:05:40,423
[Qifrey grunting]

84
00:05:47,472 --> 00:05:49,808
[woman gasps] Amazing.

85
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:51,643
I can't believe what I'm seeing!

86
00:05:51,685 --> 00:05:53,728
He parted the river
with a sword!

87
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:56,898
Remain calm and stay away
from the river!

88
00:05:57,356 --> 00:05:59,776
[QIFREY] Olruggio,
how many in the carriage?

89
00:05:59,818 --> 00:06:02,988
Only two!
I'm flying the first out now.

90
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:04,823
[Qifrey grunting]

91
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:10,369
The river isn't
making this easy. [grunts]

92
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:12,206
Thanks for that, water,
I hate you too.

93
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:15,792
Just hang in there.
On my way back.

94
00:06:18,212 --> 00:06:20,130
Got you. We're done here.

95
00:06:20,172 --> 00:06:21,464
[QIFREY] Understood.

96
00:06:23,008 --> 00:06:24,134
[Qifrey grunts]

97
00:06:26,011 --> 00:06:28,055
[yelling, grunting]

98
00:06:39,566 --> 00:06:40,734
[Qifrey sighs]

99
00:06:41,735 --> 00:06:43,070
[OLRUGGIO] Well done.

100
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,072
Everyone's safe.

101
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,365
We did all right, then.

102
00:06:50,077 --> 00:06:53,121
- [Dagda pants] Custas!
- [CUSTAS] Dagda!

103
00:06:56,415 --> 00:06:57,918
[CUSTAS] I'm sorry.

104
00:06:57,959 --> 00:07:01,129
I... I was trying to save
our equipment, but...

105
00:07:01,755 --> 00:07:02,923
Forget it.

106
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:04,674
What matters is you're safe.

107
00:07:06,551 --> 00:07:07,677
[DAGDA] You saved his life.

108
00:07:07,719 --> 00:07:09,637
I can't possibly
thank you enough!

109
00:07:09,679 --> 00:07:12,640
No need. I'm just glad
we arrived in time.

110
00:07:12,682 --> 00:07:15,102
My apprentices have brought
medicine for you,

111
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:17,062
if you're injured,
they're here to...

112
00:07:17,104 --> 00:07:18,146
[BOTH] Uh?

113
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:22,067
[COCO] Look how the water moves!
[exclaims]

114
00:07:22,109 --> 00:07:25,237
- It's sublime.
- Huh, I must say, it is.

115
00:07:25,279 --> 00:07:27,530
The greatest contraption
ever contrapted!

116
00:07:27,572 --> 00:07:30,158
Master Qifrey,
what is this contraption?

117
00:07:31,410 --> 00:07:32,493
[QIFREY] Oh, this?

118
00:07:33,161 --> 00:07:35,454
We have dubbed it
"the Raincleaver."

119
00:07:36,957 --> 00:07:39,000
The pattern inscribed
into the blade

120
00:07:39,042 --> 00:07:40,752
is made up of Casting Seals.

121
00:07:41,378 --> 00:07:43,964
Though they're quite small,
they're numerous enough

122
00:07:44,005 --> 00:07:46,507
that this blade could carve
a path through the ocean.

123
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:47,968
[Coco and Tetia gasp]

124
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:50,220
Can we give it a swing or two?

125
00:07:50,262 --> 00:07:52,097
I think it would be educational!

126
00:07:52,139 --> 00:07:53,472
I disagree.

127
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:55,183
Magically augmented weapons

128
00:07:55,225 --> 00:07:57,394
must be handled
with utmost care.

129
00:07:58,645 --> 00:08:00,272
It isn't safe,

130
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:02,983
so no more words about it
'til you're older.

131
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:04,943
[BOTH] Huh?

132
00:08:04,985 --> 00:08:06,153
[OLRUGGIO] Qifrey!

133
00:08:06,736 --> 00:08:09,739
Just to be thorough,
I think I'll look upriver.

134
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:11,325
Fair enough.

135
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:13,534
Then I'll check
the damage downriver.

136
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:15,329
Tetia, care to join?

137
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:17,372
[chuckles] Hurrah!

138
00:08:17,414 --> 00:08:19,540
- [OLRUGGIO] Richeh, with me.
- Right.

139
00:08:21,084 --> 00:08:23,544
You two stay.
Keep an eye on things here.

140
00:08:23,586 --> 00:08:24,671
Be safe now.

141
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:26,798
We will be!

142
00:08:28,633 --> 00:08:29,759
[Agott scoffs]

143
00:08:37,976 --> 00:08:40,270
[COCO] This is so awkward.

144
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:42,897
I need to hurry
and fix Agott's shoes

145
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:44,774
so I can give them back.

146
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:48,403
There. That ought to do it!

147
00:08:48,445 --> 00:08:49,612
Feels better already.

148
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:51,198
Thanks for the help,
Little Miss Witch.

149
00:08:51,239 --> 00:08:52,782
[Coco gasps]

150
00:08:53,532 --> 00:08:56,411
[COCO] Little Miss Witch?
Little Miss Witch!

151
00:08:56,453 --> 00:08:59,538
Little Miss Witch! [squeals]

152
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:01,916
[man grunts]
That's the last of it.

153
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:03,710
We lost half our cargo.

154
00:09:03,751 --> 00:09:06,963
But it certainly could have
been much worse.

155
00:09:07,506 --> 00:09:08,798
- [DAGDA] Custas!
- [MEN] Huh?

156
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:11,343
[DAGDA] No! Whatever you're
trying to do, it's not worth it!

157
00:09:11,385 --> 00:09:12,802
Come back!

158
00:09:12,844 --> 00:09:15,013
It's fine,
the water's calm here!

159
00:09:15,055 --> 00:09:17,098
See? There's a nook
in the riverbank.

160
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:19,809
And some of our stuff
got caught in the eddy.

161
00:09:19,851 --> 00:09:22,229
I'll come back up
as soon as I've grabbed it.

162
00:09:24,898 --> 00:09:26,191
Don't be a fool!

163
00:09:26,233 --> 00:09:27,484
The bank is unstable there.

164
00:09:27,526 --> 00:09:29,236
That's why that nook exists!

165
00:09:29,277 --> 00:09:31,279
Get back here this instant!

166
00:09:31,321 --> 00:09:32,613
Custas!

167
00:09:35,367 --> 00:09:36,326
[Coco gasps]

168
00:09:36,368 --> 00:09:38,036
[all gasp]

169
00:09:48,422 --> 00:09:50,090
♪

170
00:09:53,051 --> 00:09:56,846
No. This can't be... Custas.

171
00:09:57,264 --> 00:09:59,307
[AGOTT] Wait, Mr. Dagda.
You can't!

172
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:01,184
[MAN] You could cause
another landslide!

173
00:10:01,226 --> 00:10:02,519
- Stop!
- Let go of me!

174
00:10:02,561 --> 00:10:05,355
- That's my son! Custas!
- [COCO] Agott!

175
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:10,318
[AGOTT] Coco?

176
00:10:11,361 --> 00:10:12,946
She was buri...

177
00:10:12,987 --> 00:10:14,489
- [COCO] Agott!
- [Agott gasps]

178
00:10:14,531 --> 00:10:16,908
[COCO] I'm here! Over here!

179
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:19,702
Coco, are you all right?

180
00:10:19,744 --> 00:10:21,746
Were you hurt at all?
Can you get out?

181
00:10:21,788 --> 00:10:24,832
I think I'll be okay, for now.

182
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:26,709
But, uh...

183
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:30,046
Custas, say something, please!

184
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:32,924
Custas? [whimpers]

185
00:10:32,966 --> 00:10:35,051
Custas!

186
00:10:35,969 --> 00:10:38,763
No. Please, no. [cries]

187
00:10:38,805 --> 00:10:40,181
What do I...

188
00:10:40,390 --> 00:10:41,391
What?

189
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:44,144
Oh, of course.

190
00:10:45,270 --> 00:10:47,188
There's a witch right here.

191
00:10:47,230 --> 00:10:48,731
- It's not over!
- [AGOTT] Huh?

192
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:50,150
[DAGDA] Right?

193
00:10:50,317 --> 00:10:53,320
You can use magic
to help him, can't you?

194
00:10:53,361 --> 00:10:55,696
Please, I'm begging you!

195
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:57,491
Save my son!

196
00:10:57,865 --> 00:10:59,117
[Agott gasps]

197
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:02,870
[AGOTT] This is my chance.

198
00:11:03,288 --> 00:11:05,081
Our masters aren't here,

199
00:11:05,332 --> 00:11:08,084
and I can't call them back
without my Sylph Shoes.

200
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:11,754
Coco's locked down,
and the situation is desperate.

201
00:11:12,422 --> 00:11:14,841
If I save this boy with magic,

202
00:11:14,882 --> 00:11:17,844
I can prove that they were
all wrong about me.

203
00:11:17,885 --> 00:11:19,220
[MAN] Miss Witch?

204
00:11:19,262 --> 00:11:21,097
Please, is there some spell

205
00:11:21,139 --> 00:11:23,266
- that you can use to save him?
- [AGOTT] Uh...

206
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:26,102
[MAN 1] There must be something
you can do for him, right?

207
00:11:26,144 --> 00:11:28,104
[MAN 2] I wonder what magic
we'll see this time.

208
00:11:28,146 --> 00:11:29,688
[WOMAN] How are you
focused on that?

209
00:11:29,730 --> 00:11:31,358
Custas is in danger!

210
00:11:31,399 --> 00:11:32,651
[Agott breathes shakily]

211
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:34,611
[OLD MAN] Go on, Agott.

212
00:11:34,653 --> 00:11:36,863
- Prove your worth.
- [Agott gasps]

213
00:11:38,365 --> 00:11:41,826
[WITCH 1] This is the best magic
she can muster.

214
00:11:44,371 --> 00:11:47,457
[WITCH 2] Hmm. It doesn't quite
compare to the other children's.

215
00:11:47,499 --> 00:11:49,250
[FEMALE WITCH 1] Aren't you
taking this seriously?

216
00:11:49,292 --> 00:11:51,628
[FEMALE WITCH 2] Perhaps
she's just a bit mediocre.

217
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:53,921
[WITCH 2] Are we sure
that this is her daughter?

218
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:55,089
[FEMALE WITCH 1]
If the child had talent,

219
00:11:55,131 --> 00:11:56,633
we would have seen it by now.

220
00:11:56,675 --> 00:11:59,135
[overlapping chatter]

221
00:12:00,679 --> 00:12:02,889
[ADINA] I had
high hopes for you.

222
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:05,350
But you've disappointed me,
Agott.

223
00:12:05,392 --> 00:12:07,977
You'll not be my apprentice.

224
00:12:08,019 --> 00:12:11,565
We've no need for dull children
in this family.

225
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:13,816
[Agott cries]

226
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:18,946
[AGOTT] Why does my mind
go there now?

227
00:12:18,988 --> 00:12:21,782
At a time like this! Why?

228
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:25,953
- [COCO] Agott!
- [Agott gasps]

229
00:12:25,995 --> 00:12:28,415
[COCO] What can I do?

230
00:12:29,332 --> 00:12:31,125
There must be something.

231
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:33,420
Tell me how I can help
from here!

232
00:12:36,256 --> 00:12:38,633
I need a way to save Custas!

233
00:12:38,675 --> 00:12:41,595
So tell me! Tell me what to do!

234
00:12:41,636 --> 00:12:43,054
[Agott gasps]

235
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:46,140
If you truly wish
to be useful here and now,

236
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:49,227
you should take a moment
to reconsider

237
00:12:49,269 --> 00:12:51,145
what magic is for.

238
00:12:51,605 --> 00:12:53,022
[Agott grunts softly]

239
00:12:53,481 --> 00:12:55,233
Coco, can you move?

240
00:12:55,275 --> 00:12:57,944
Describe the situation!
What do you see?

241
00:12:57,985 --> 00:12:59,237
[COCO] I see...

242
00:12:59,279 --> 00:13:00,697
I see a...

243
00:13:01,197 --> 00:13:03,366
I'm in a pocket
of the riverbank,

244
00:13:03,408 --> 00:13:05,910
and the current's
a lot slower here.

245
00:13:05,952 --> 00:13:08,121
I don't think
it'll sweep me away, but...

246
00:13:08,162 --> 00:13:09,914
It's so muddy.

247
00:13:09,956 --> 00:13:11,458
I keep slipping!

248
00:13:11,499 --> 00:13:13,752
I don't think I can climb out.

249
00:13:13,792 --> 00:13:15,836
Custas is knocked out.

250
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:18,339
And the rock he's under
looks too big to move,

251
00:13:18,381 --> 00:13:20,007
even for an adult.

252
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:23,344
Also...

253
00:13:24,471 --> 00:13:25,555
[gasps]

254
00:13:26,473 --> 00:13:28,057
[AGOTT] Even if her components
were dry,

255
00:13:28,099 --> 00:13:30,518
these people
don't know our secret.

256
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,562
We can't let them see us draw.

257
00:13:33,313 --> 00:13:35,482
What now, Agott?

258
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:37,816
[AGOTT] I don't know.

259
00:13:44,449 --> 00:13:45,700
[footsteps]

260
00:13:46,493 --> 00:13:47,868
[LULUCI] Easthies...

261
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:50,913
We've received reports
from a village near Kalhn.

262
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:53,750
[GALGA] Multiple sightings
of a huge pillar of water.

263
00:13:53,792 --> 00:13:55,960
Somewhere in the Marshwoods
upriver.

264
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:58,963
Let's go, then.

265
00:14:03,426 --> 00:14:05,970
[AGOTT]
Dire as the situation may seem,

266
00:14:06,012 --> 00:14:07,639
Coco still hasn't given up.

267
00:14:07,681 --> 00:14:09,182
[Coco pants]

268
00:14:11,559 --> 00:14:13,936
[COCO]
If I could just use magic.

269
00:14:14,729 --> 00:14:17,524
- [gasps] Hey, Agott!
- [AGOTT] Hm?

270
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:20,443
[COCO] Um, I need those things!

271
00:14:20,485 --> 00:14:21,528
[AGOTT] What?

272
00:14:21,569 --> 00:14:23,237
I forgot the name!

273
00:14:23,279 --> 00:14:26,115
The things! Master Olruggio's
inventions?

274
00:14:26,157 --> 00:14:27,283
The two rings!

275
00:14:27,325 --> 00:14:29,536
[gasps] Oh, yes.

276
00:14:29,577 --> 00:14:31,078
The Link Rings!

277
00:14:33,289 --> 00:14:35,416
That sorts half our problem.

278
00:14:36,042 --> 00:14:37,794
[COCO]
Once my Spell Quire's dry,

279
00:14:37,836 --> 00:14:39,253
I can use
the new spell I learned

280
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:40,547
to levitate the rock.

281
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:43,174
And then, I'll be able
to save Custas!

282
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:47,886
[AGOTT] Trouble is...
Coco still can't do it.

283
00:14:47,928 --> 00:14:49,848
The only permissible way

284
00:14:49,888 --> 00:14:51,932
to compose a spell
in front of Outsiders

285
00:14:52,392 --> 00:14:53,852
is to draw
with your pen and paper

286
00:14:53,892 --> 00:14:55,729
hidden in the folds
of your cloak.

287
00:14:56,688 --> 00:14:58,189
That requires muscle memory.

288
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:00,899
Countless hours of practice.

289
00:15:00,941 --> 00:15:02,109
[Agott gasps]

290
00:15:02,819 --> 00:15:04,195
[inhales deeply]

291
00:15:04,487 --> 00:15:05,655
[Agott grunts softly]

292
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:09,409
[MAN 1] Is she going
to do something?

293
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:10,951
[WOMAN] Maybe she needs
more time because she's young...

294
00:15:10,993 --> 00:15:12,871
- [AGOTT] Your attention please.
- [ALL] Uh?

295
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:18,125
[AGOTT]
I am Qifrey's top apprentice,

296
00:15:18,167 --> 00:15:21,212
I am known
as Agott Arklaum.

297
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:24,131
And I offer you
this demonstration

298
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:26,259
of the power residing within me!

299
00:15:28,887 --> 00:15:31,013
[AGOTT]
Countless hours of practice,

300
00:15:31,055 --> 00:15:33,140
so that when the time
came to act,

301
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:35,142
I wouldn't be frozen by fear.

302
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:39,522
Even if Coco can't do this...

303
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:42,024
I can!

304
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:44,736
[all grunting]

305
00:15:44,778 --> 00:15:45,944
♪

306
00:15:51,284 --> 00:15:52,786
[all gasp]

307
00:15:59,459 --> 00:16:01,461
Beautiful.

308
00:16:06,466 --> 00:16:08,134
[both grunt]

309
00:16:09,677 --> 00:16:11,512
[COCO] I was just
practicing levitation

310
00:16:11,554 --> 00:16:12,639
with the carapace yams.

311
00:16:14,599 --> 00:16:17,268
This can work. I can do it.

312
00:16:22,981 --> 00:16:24,400
Then again...

313
00:16:25,192 --> 00:16:28,195
That seal struggled
to make a yam float.

314
00:16:28,237 --> 00:16:30,907
So I know it can't lift
a boulder this huge.

315
00:16:30,949 --> 00:16:34,160
Not with a seal as small
as a Palm Quire.

316
00:16:34,201 --> 00:16:35,536
- [Custas grunts softly]
- [COCO] Uh?

317
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:38,247
[COCO] Custas!

318
00:16:38,790 --> 00:16:41,125
Where am I? What happened?

319
00:16:41,167 --> 00:16:43,753
[COCO] You're awake!
What a relief.

320
00:16:44,504 --> 00:16:46,965
- [CUSTAS] Who are you?
- My name is Coco.

321
00:16:47,005 --> 00:16:48,215
I'm a witch.

322
00:16:48,257 --> 00:16:50,635
We both fell
when the bank collapsed.

323
00:16:50,677 --> 00:16:51,719
You remember?

324
00:16:51,761 --> 00:16:52,929
Huh...

325
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:57,475
So, then,
I guess I'm still alive.

326
00:16:57,934 --> 00:17:00,269
When I saw that bird
of light in the sky,

327
00:17:00,854 --> 00:17:02,605
I thought I was dead for sure.

328
00:17:02,647 --> 00:17:05,566
Oh, the bird?
No, it's nothing like that.

329
00:17:05,608 --> 00:17:07,527
It's just a spell
that my friend cast!

330
00:17:07,986 --> 00:17:11,280
[gasps softly]
A spell my friend cast.

331
00:17:11,322 --> 00:17:12,782
Wait, that's it!

332
00:17:15,201 --> 00:17:17,829
[AGOTT] This won't distract them
for much longer.

333
00:17:17,871 --> 00:17:19,330
Hurry, Coco!

334
00:17:19,664 --> 00:17:20,748
[MAN] Miss.

335
00:17:20,832 --> 00:17:23,083
That spell's certainly nice
to look at,

336
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:24,711
but what does it do?

337
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:26,921
[DAGDA] All you did
was put on a light show!

338
00:17:26,963 --> 00:17:28,673
That bird isn't helping
with anything!

339
00:17:28,715 --> 00:17:31,133
Can't you make it carry me
down there?

340
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:32,886
Or could it pry him loose
somehow

341
00:17:32,927 --> 00:17:34,345
and fly him to safety?

342
00:17:34,387 --> 00:17:35,972
Sorry, I...

343
00:17:36,014 --> 00:17:39,517
[DAGDA] Enough! I'll climb down
and save him myself!

344
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:41,561
[AGOTT]
If he looks down there now...

345
00:17:42,144 --> 00:17:44,480
[AGOTT] No! Don't do it.
You mustn't!

346
00:17:44,981 --> 00:17:46,024
[Dagda gasps]

347
00:17:46,064 --> 00:17:47,149
[Agott gasps]

348
00:17:49,067 --> 00:17:51,529
- [wind howling]
- [Coco breathes shakily]

349
00:17:56,116 --> 00:18:00,580
[COCO] Pull me in, please!
I... I can't get down!

350
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:02,665
- [Coco exclaims]
- [Dagda grunts]

351
00:18:02,707 --> 00:18:03,875
[thudding]

352
00:18:03,917 --> 00:18:06,669
- [all exclaim]
- [DAGDA] Custas! Custas!

353
00:18:06,711 --> 00:18:08,337
- [MAN] Dagda, can we help?
- Custas!

354
00:18:08,838 --> 00:18:10,172
[indistinct chatter]

355
00:18:10,214 --> 00:18:12,258
- [MAN 1] How is he?
- [MAN 2] What can we do?

356
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:17,597
[indistinct chatter]

357
00:18:18,681 --> 00:18:20,641
[COCO] It's still floating!

358
00:18:20,683 --> 00:18:22,769
- It won't stop!
- Coco, how did you...

359
00:18:23,394 --> 00:18:24,520
Uh...

360
00:18:27,065 --> 00:18:28,691
[exclaims softly]

361
00:18:29,067 --> 00:18:31,027
Agott! Agott!

362
00:18:31,069 --> 00:18:32,152
What're you...

363
00:18:32,445 --> 00:18:35,031
[COCO] Thank goodness
it worked! I was so scared!

364
00:18:36,282 --> 00:18:38,576
I'm so... so glad.

365
00:18:39,035 --> 00:18:40,703
We did it, Agott!

366
00:18:40,745 --> 00:18:43,205
Let go of me
and pull yourself together!

367
00:18:43,247 --> 00:18:46,793
Now explain, how did you manage
to deal with that massive rock?

368
00:18:49,003 --> 00:18:50,838
Hold on. What is this?

369
00:18:51,756 --> 00:18:53,173
Sand?

370
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:54,717
[COCO] Mm-hmm.

371
00:18:54,759 --> 00:18:56,719
I remembered how
with the dragon,

372
00:18:56,761 --> 00:18:59,555
you and Richeh saved us
with a rock-breaking spell.

373
00:19:00,807 --> 00:19:02,642
Right, of course!

374
00:19:03,101 --> 00:19:05,019
Even with smaller Seals,

375
00:19:05,061 --> 00:19:07,605
the Wall Breaker spell could
easily crush that boulder

376
00:19:07,647 --> 00:19:09,857
without hurting the person
beneath it.

377
00:19:09,899 --> 00:19:11,484
[COCO] Exactly.

378
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:14,028
I couldn't do anything
but watch back then.

379
00:19:14,737 --> 00:19:16,280
But I learned from my friends,

380
00:19:16,322 --> 00:19:17,949
and picked up your spells.

381
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:20,785
I never could've done this
on my own.

382
00:19:21,869 --> 00:19:24,497
Your shining bird reminded me!

383
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:27,583
You really saved the day, Agott!
Thank you!

384
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:31,963
That shining distress beacon
was to call our masters back.

385
00:19:32,005 --> 00:19:34,590
The fact that it was helpful
to you is incidental.

386
00:19:34,632 --> 00:19:37,343
And also, you and I
are not friends!

387
00:19:37,384 --> 00:19:38,970
[wind howling]

388
00:19:43,307 --> 00:19:45,935
[COCO] I really am so glad.

389
00:19:46,686 --> 00:19:49,105
We managed to save him.

390
00:19:50,481 --> 00:19:53,567
Maybe someday, I'll save my mom.

391
00:19:56,946 --> 00:19:58,072
I will.

392
00:19:58,364 --> 00:19:59,740
I know it.

393
00:20:02,535 --> 00:20:03,995
Coco...

394
00:20:04,037 --> 00:20:05,997
[wind blowing]

395
00:20:13,046 --> 00:20:14,463
[both gasp]

396
00:20:14,839 --> 00:20:16,799
[both grunting]

397
00:20:20,469 --> 00:20:23,139
What... What are these things?

398
00:20:23,181 --> 00:20:25,808
Silverwhite Capture Pennants,
I think.

399
00:20:26,893 --> 00:20:29,812
Along with scarlet cloaks,

400
00:20:30,354 --> 00:20:32,065
and winged caps.

401
00:20:33,691 --> 00:20:35,068
They're really here.

402
00:20:36,027 --> 00:20:38,029
The Knights Moralis!

403
00:20:38,071 --> 00:20:39,822
[EASTHIES] Who are you?

404
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,615
You there...

405
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:43,659
Were you the one
who cast that spell?

406
00:20:43,701 --> 00:20:44,785
[Coco gasps]

407
00:20:44,827 --> 00:20:47,163
[EASTHIES]
Or are you the culprit?

408
00:20:48,039 --> 00:20:51,084
Children or not,
you'll be granted no mercy.

409
00:20:51,125 --> 00:20:52,292
Now, speak.

410
00:20:52,877 --> 00:20:55,337
Which of you is in league
with the Brimmed Caps?

411
00:20:55,838 --> 00:20:57,215
What are you on about?

412
00:20:57,255 --> 00:20:59,592
We don't have anything to do
with the Brimmed Caps!

413
00:20:59,633 --> 00:21:01,844
And none of the magic we used
was forbidden!

414
00:21:01,886 --> 00:21:04,513
We only cast spells
that help people!

415
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:06,640
- [EASTHIES] Is that so?
- [AGOTT] Huh?

416
00:21:07,225 --> 00:21:08,726
Then what happened there?

417
00:21:09,936 --> 00:21:11,145
[Agott gasps]

418
00:21:11,437 --> 00:21:12,813
[Coco breathes shakily]

419
00:21:13,397 --> 00:21:14,607
[COCO] What...

420
00:21:18,111 --> 00:21:19,237
[COCO] What is this?

421
00:21:20,154 --> 00:21:22,240
What happened?

422
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:25,952
It didn't stop at the rock.

423
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:27,828
The whole riverbed...

424
00:21:27,870 --> 00:21:30,706
The whole area turned to sand.

425
00:21:31,415 --> 00:21:34,210
It's even crushing
the river to mist.

426
00:21:34,668 --> 00:21:36,587
[MAN] What is this?

427
00:21:36,629 --> 00:21:41,259
[COCO]
No, my spell couldn't do this.

428
00:21:41,299 --> 00:21:42,927
- [EASTHIES] I see.
- [gasps]

429
00:21:42,969 --> 00:21:45,888
[EASTHIES] So you admit
the spell was yours.

430
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:48,808
A novice could not wield
such power.

431
00:21:48,849 --> 00:21:50,434
Unless, of course,

432
00:21:50,476 --> 00:21:53,854
she obtained that power
by committing a violation.

433
00:21:54,147 --> 00:21:55,648
[Coco breathes shakily]

434
00:21:55,689 --> 00:21:59,152
[EASTHIES] The laws of the Pact
are absolute.

435
00:21:59,193 --> 00:22:02,113
I hereby relieve you
of your memories.

436
00:22:02,155 --> 00:22:03,363
[Coco gasps]

437
00:22:06,117 --> 00:22:09,162
[♪ closing theme song playing]

